# Build and Test

Read `docs/VERIFICATION.md` and starting `git status --short`. Determine the affected modules and run the smallest relevant check, then required target/suite checks and builds.

Use only verified repository commands. Do not install tools, change signing/dependencies/configuration, clean user files, or edit production code merely to make verification pass unless the user explicitly expands the task.

Separate implementation failures from environment failures. Build does not replace tests. Finish with `git diff --check` and relevant diff/status review.

Report command, scope, pass/fail/not-run, decisive error, manual checks, and residual risk. State completion only when every required check passes.
